msgid "News: Quarkus 3.36 Platform Release"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This summary was generated using AI, reviewed by humans - https://youtube."
"com/live/EczihvU1gG8[watch the video] for the full story."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In episode 249 of Quarkus Insights, Philip Krüger from Australia joined the "
"team to demonstrate how coding agents can enhance the https://quarkus.io/"
"[Quarkus] developer experience. Despite battling flu season and joining at "
"11 PM his time, Philip showcased the new https://github.com/quarkusio/"
"quarkus-agent-mcp[Quarkus Agent MCP] server and how it enables AI-powered "
"development workflows."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Before diving into coding agents, the team announced the https://quarkus.io/"
"blog/quarkus-3-36-released/[Quarkus 3.36 platform release], which includes:"
msgstr ""

msgid "**OIDC Spiffe authentication"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Signals** - a new eventing infrastructure"
msgstr ""

msgid "Enhanced developer experience features"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For those interested in the design decisions behind signals, the team "
"recorded a https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_VY9G_DMFjw[detailed "
"presentation] during the Quarkus community call with extensive discussion "
"about the architecture and future direction."
msgstr ""

msgid "The Evolution: From Dev UI to AI Experience"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Philip explained the journey from developer-focused tools to AI-focused "
"tools:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Dev UI Foundation"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://quarkus.io/guides/dev-ui[Dev UI] provides developers with a web "
"console to access services on their running application in dev mode. This "
"has been a core part of Quarkus's developer experience pillar."
msgstr ""

msgid "Chappie: AI-Enhanced Developer Experience"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://github.com/quarkiverse/quarkus-chappie[Chappie] emerged to enhance "
"the developer experience using AI, integrating with Dev UI and other "
"components like error screens. Key features include:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Chat interface within Dev UI"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation) integration with Quarkus documentation"
msgstr ""

msgid "Version-aware documentation access"
msgstr ""

msgid "CLI support for AI interactions"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Important**: Chappie is still actively maintained and focuses on enhancing "
"the developer experience through Dev UI and other channels."
msgstr ""

msgid "MCP: The Bridge to Coding Agents"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When https://modelcontextprotocol.io/[Model Context Protocol (MCP)] emerged, "
"the team realized it shared a similar architecture with Dev UI (both use "
"JSON-RPC for client-server communication). This made it straightforward to "
"expose Dev UI's backend as an MCP server."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"However, this revealed a critical insight: **the user had changed**. Instead "
"of targeting developers directly, the tools now needed to serve coding "
"agents, requiring a shift from \"developer experience\" (DevX) to \"AI "
"experience\" (AIX)."
msgstr ""

msgid "The Quarkus Agent MCP Server"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Philip demonstrated the https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus-agent-"
"mcp[Quarkus Agent MCP] server, a standalone tool designed specifically for "
"coding agents building Quarkus applications."
msgstr ""

msgid "Key Advantages Over Dev MCP"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Decoupled from Applications**:\n"
"- Runs as a standalone MCP server\n"
"- Can create applications (doesn't require an existing app)\n"
"- Remains available even when applications crash\n"
"- Supports the full application lifecycle"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Optimized Tool Management**:\n"
"- Uses a \"search tools\" pattern instead of exposing hundreds of individual "
"tools\n"
"- Tools are discovered dynamically based on installed extensions\n"
"- Reduces context window usage for LLMs"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Documentation Integration**:\n"
"- RAG access to Quarkus documentation\n"
"- Version-aware documentation\n"
"- Support for extension-specific documentation\n"
"- Includes documentation from transitive dependencies (like https://"
"hibernate.org/[Hibernate])"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Skills System**:\n"
"- Extension-specific skills guide the agent\n"
"- Skills are version-controlled with Quarkus releases\n"
"- Can be customized at user or project level"
msgstr ""

msgid "Installation and Setup"
msgstr ""

msgid "The Quarkus Agent MCP is available through multiple channels:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Via Claude Marketplace**:\n"
"Simply install from the marketplace in https://claude.ai/[Claude Desktop]."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Manual Configuration** (using https://www.jbang.dev/[JBang]):"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Local Development** (using Java):"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The server works with various AI harnesses including Claude, https://github."
"com/Pythagora-io/gpt-pilot[GPT Pilot], https://www.cursor.com/[Cursor], and "
"others that support MCP."
msgstr ""

msgid "Live Demo: Building a Vinyl Collection Manager"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Philip demonstrated the agent in action by asking it to create a vinyl "
"collection management application:"
msgstr ""

msgid "The agent automatically:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Selected the tech stack**: Chose Quarkus without being explicitly told "
"(due to the MCP context)"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Refined requirements**: Asked clarifying questions about database and UI "
"preferences"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Created the application**: Used the Quarkus CLI through MCP tools"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Built the features**: Implemented CRUD operations with https://www."
"postgresql.org/[PostgreSQL] backend"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Added a web UI**: Created a static HTML/JavaScript interface"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Tested the application**: Verified functionality using browser automation"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The entire process happened with minimal intervention, showcasing how the "
"agent leverages the MCP tools to understand Quarkus conventions and best "
"practices."
msgstr ""

msgid "Available Tools in Quarkus Agent MCP"
msgstr ""

msgid "Philip outlined the tool categories available to coding agents:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Application Lifecycle Tools"
msgstr ""

msgid "`create_application` - Bootstrap new Quarkus projects"
msgstr ""

msgid "`start_application` - Start applications in dev mode"
msgstr ""

msgid "`stop_application` - Stop running applications"
msgstr ""

msgid "`restart_application` - Restart applications"
msgstr ""

msgid "`application_status` - Check application state"
msgstr ""

msgid "`open_browser` - Open Dev UI or application in browser"
msgstr ""

msgid "Knowledge Tools"
msgstr ""

msgid "`search_docs` - Search Quarkus documentation with RAG"
msgstr ""

msgid "`get_skills` - Access extension-specific skills"
msgstr ""

msgid "`list_skills` - View available skills"
msgstr ""

msgid "Dev MCP Integration"
msgstr ""

msgid "`search_tools` - Discover available Dev MCP tools dynamically"
msgstr ""

msgid "`call_tool` - Execute Dev MCP tools (proxied through)"
msgstr ""

msgid "Logging and Debugging"
msgstr ""

msgid "`get_logs` - Access application logs"
msgstr ""

msgid "`set_log_level` - Adjust logging verbosity"
msgstr ""

msgid "Skill Customization"
msgstr ""

msgid "`save_skill` - Persist skills locally"
msgstr ""

msgid "`update_skill` - Modify existing skills"
msgstr ""

msgid "`install_quarkus_skills` - Install official Quarkus skills"
msgstr ""

msgid "The Skills System"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Skills are markdown files that guide coding agents on how to work with "
"specific Quarkus features."
msgstr ""

msgid "Extension Skills"
msgstr ""

msgid "Each Quarkus extension can provide a skill that includes:"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Metadata**: Extension name, description, documentation URL"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Usage patterns**: How to use the extension effectively"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Best practices**: Quarkus-specific conventions"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Available tools**: What Dev MCP methods are available"
msgstr ""

msgid "Example skill structure:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Skill Generation Process"
msgstr ""

msgid "Philip described an interesting approach to generating skills:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Start two AI instances (one with https://www.anthropic.com/claude[Claude "
"Sonnet], one with Claude Opus)"
msgstr ""

msgid "Have Sonnet attempt to build a feature (e.g., GraphQL endpoint)"
msgstr ""

msgid "When Sonnet struggles, ask Opus for help"
msgstr ""

msgid "Ask Opus to generate a skill based on what it learned"
msgstr ""

msgid "Test the skill with Sonnet to validate effectiveness"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This iterative process helps create skills that genuinely improve agent "
"performance."
msgstr ""

msgid "Skills can be customized at different levels:"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Project-level**: Saved in `.quarkus/skills/` directory"
msgstr ""

msgid "**User-level**: Saved in user's home directory"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Enhancement mode**: Add organization-specific guidance without replacing "
"the base skill:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Documentation Integration"
msgstr ""

msgid "The documentation system has evolved significantly:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Current Approach (Chappie)"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Chappie builds a vector database from documentation, exports it, and "
"publishes it as a Docker image. Dev services download this image when needed."
""
msgstr ""

msgid "New Approach (Quarkus 3.37+)"
msgstr ""

msgid "Starting with the next release:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Maven plugin**: Extensions use a Maven plugin to generate vector database "
"SQL exports from their documentation"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Aggregation**: The agent MCP aggregates documentation from all extensions "
"and dependencies"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Broader coverage**: Includes documentation for libraries like Hibernate, "
"not just Quarkus extensions"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This approach is more distributable and supports the full dependency tree."
msgstr ""

msgid "RAG vs. Direct Documentation"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Philip questioned whether RAG is still necessary, given modern LLMs' large "
"context windows. The team discussed trade-offs:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**RAG Benefits**:\n"
"- Reduces context window usage\n"
"- Provides focused, relevant information\n"
"- Works with smaller models"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Direct Documentation**:\n"
"- Simpler implementation\n"
"- No vector database maintenance\n"
"- Better for comprehensive understanding"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The team continues to evaluate the best approach as LLM capabilities evolve."
msgstr ""

msgid "Extension Developer Guide"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For extension maintainers, Philip outlined what's needed to support AI "
"experience:"
msgstr ""

msgid "1. Review Dev MCP Methods"
msgstr ""

msgid "Ensure Dev MCP methods target AI use cases, not just human developers:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Example - Continuous Testing**:\n"
"- **For humans**: Toggle continuous testing on/off\n"
"- **For agents**: Run tests at specific points in time"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Example - Hot Reload**:\n"
"- **For humans**: Automatic reload on file changes\n"
"- **For agents**: Explicit reload command when ready"
msgstr ""

msgid "2. Add Extension Skills"
msgstr ""

msgid "Create a skill file in your extension:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The skill should include:\n"
"- Clear description of the extension's purpose\n"
"- Usage patterns and examples\n"
"- Common pitfalls and solutions\n"
"- Integration points with other extensions"
msgstr ""

msgid "3. Ensure Documentation Quality"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Make sure your extension's documentation is:\n"
"- Accurate and up-to-date\n"
"- Well-structured with clear headings\n"
"- Includes practical examples\n"
"- Links to related documentation"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For core Quarkus extensions, documentation is already integrated. For https:/"
"/github.com/quarkiverse[Quarkiverse] extensions, add this to your POM:"
msgstr ""

msgid "4. Follow the Extension Maturity Matrix"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The https://quarkus.io/guides/extension-maturity-matrix[Extension Maturity "
"Matrix] now includes AI experience criteria. Following these guidelines "
"ensures your extension works well with coding agents."
msgstr ""

msgid "Team&#8217;s AI Development Practices"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In response to questions on the live-stream chat, the team shared their "
"diverse approaches to AI-assisted development:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Tools and Models Used"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**IDEs and Harnesses**:\n"
"- https://claude.ai/[Claude Desktop] (most popular)\n"
"- https://www.jetbrains.com/idea/[IntelliJ IDEA] with AI Assistant\n"
"- https://bob.ibm.com/\n"
"- https://www.cursor.com/[Cursor]\n"
"- https://github.com/Pythagora-io/gpt-pilot[GPT Pilot]\n"
"- https://www.jetbrains.com/qodana/[JetBrains Qodana]"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Models**:\n"
"- Claude (Sonnet and Opus)\n"
"- https://github.com/features/copilot[GitHub Copilot]\n"
"- https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api[Google Gemini]"
msgstr ""

msgid "Workflow Patterns"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Philip's Approach**:\n"
"- Uses Claude Desktop exclusively\n"
"- Views code through Dev UI's workspace browser\n"
"- Treats the agent as a soundboard for design discussions\n"
"- Runs multiple Claude instances for different tasks\n"
"- Rarely opens a traditional IDE"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Max's Approach**:\n"
"- Prefers https://github.com/Pythagora-io/gpt-pilot[GPT Pilot]\n"
"- Focuses on incremental development\n"
"- Uses plan mode but avoids over-planning\n"
"- Emphasizes iterative refinement"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Eric's Approach**:\n"
"- Uses IntelliJ with Claude integration\n"
"- Leverages IDE context sensitivity\n"
"- Benefits from IDE's diff viewer\n"
"- Combines IDE refactoring with AI generation"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Holly's Approach**:\n"
"- Swaps between Claude Code and Bob\n"
"- Uses Test-Driven Development (TDD) with agents\n"
"- Writes tests first, then has agent implement\n"
"- Finds TDD particularly effective for reproducers"
msgstr ""

msgid "Common Themes"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Not necessarily faster for new features**: AI doesn't dramatically speed "
"up complex feature development"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Excellent for maintenance**: Fixing bugs, updating dependencies, handling "
"CI failures"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Great for boilerplate**: Generating repetitive code structures"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Requires review**: All code is reviewed before merging"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Reduces mental load**: Handles tedious tasks while developers focus on "
"design"
msgstr ""

msgid "Babysitting vs. Collaboration"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The team discussed the evolution from \"babysitting\" agents to true "
"collaboration:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Six Months Ago"
msgstr ""

msgid "Approve every single change"
msgstr ""

msgid "Watch every step"
msgstr ""

msgid "Constant intervention required"
msgstr ""

msgid "Today"
msgstr ""

msgid "Outline the approach"
msgstr ""

msgid "Let the agent work independently"
msgstr ""

msgid "Review the final result"
msgstr ""

msgid "Treat it like a skilled junior developer"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Key insight**: Modern agents can work autonomously on well-defined tasks, "
"but still require human review and guidance on architecture decisions."
msgstr ""

msgid "Test-Driven Development with Agents"
msgstr ""

msgid "Holly emphasized the value of TDD when working with agents:"
msgstr ""

msgid "The TDD Workflow"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Write the test first**: Define expected behavior"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Verify it fails**: Ensure the test catches the issue"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Have agent implement**: Let the agent write code to pass the test"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Review the solution**: Ensure quality and correctness"
msgstr ""

msgid "Benefits"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Focused tests**: Tests target specific functionality, not just coverage"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Better reproducers**: Excellent for bug reports and issue reproduction"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Guided development**: Tests provide clear success criteria"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Reduced boilerplate**: Agents handle test setup code"
msgstr ""

msgid "Caveat"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Asking agents to \"write tests\" without guidance often produces low-value "
"tests that are \"paid by the line.\" TDD keeps tests meaningful and "
"purposeful."
msgstr ""

msgid "Spec-Driven Development"
msgstr ""

msgid "Philip and Max advocated for spending more time on specifications:"
msgstr ""

msgid "The Spec-First Approach"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Define the plan**: Outline architecture and approach"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Persist the plan**: Save it for reference"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Follow the plan**: Have the agent implement according to spec"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Iterate on the plan**: Refine based on results"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Better results**: More time planning = better implementation"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Clearer communication**: Specs serve as documentation"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Easier review**: Reviewers understand the intent"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Reusable patterns**: Specs can be adapted for similar features"
msgstr ""

msgid "When to Use Coding Agents"
msgstr ""

msgid "The team shared guidance on when agents provide the most value:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Excellent Use Cases"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Bug fixes**: Especially with clear reproducers"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Dependency updates**: Handling breaking changes"
msgstr ""

msgid "**CI/CD maintenance**: Fixing build failures"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Boilerplate generation**: CRUD operations, DTOs, mappers"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Documentation**: Generating or updating docs"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Refactoring**: Mechanical code transformations"
msgstr ""

msgid "Less Effective Use Cases"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Complex architecture decisions**: Still requires human judgment"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Novel algorithms**: Agents struggle with truly new approaches"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Performance optimization**: Requires deep understanding"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Security-critical code**: Needs expert review"
msgstr ""

msgid "The \"Soundboard\" Pattern"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Philip highlighted using agents as a soundboard for design discussions, "
"especially valuable when working across time zones without human colleagues "
"available."
msgstr ""

msgid "Challenges and Future Directions"
msgstr ""

msgid "Current Challenges"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Non-deterministic behavior**: Same prompt can produce different results, "
"making testing difficult."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Rapid evolution**: The AI landscape changes quickly, requiring constant "
"adaptation."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Tool proliferation**: Managing the growing ecosystem of AI tools and "
"approaches."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Context management**: Balancing between providing enough context and "
"overwhelming the model."
msgstr ""

msgid "Future Improvements"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Better sandboxing**: The team mentioned https://github.com/Sanne/incus-"
"spawn[Incus Spawn] for safer agent execution."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Skill refinement**: Continuing to improve extension skills based on real-"
"world usage."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Documentation evolution**: Determining the right balance between RAG and "
"direct documentation access."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Tool consolidation**: Potentially combining or removing redundant tools."
msgstr ""

